    [CI][Docker] Update flash-attention-npu pin for v0.32.0rc (#20523)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Update the flash-attention-npu source pin in the A2/A3 Ubuntu and
    openEuler Dockerfiles on `releases/v0.32.0rc` from
    `9c9f00648fa150e84228a9b757990485fc670df3` to
    `2e5320494cb474365bacaf42c94abf0c7de0affc`.
    
    The old commit is the tip of upstream's `v0.4.2.post2` branch, not an
    ancestor of current `main`. The new commit is upstream `main` HEAD
    verified on 2026-11-01 (`update package version to 0.5.0`). Keep the
    existing clone, submodule initialization, and source installation steps,
    with a full SHA for reproducibility.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. A2/A3 Ubuntu and openEuler images build flash-attention-npu from
    the updated main snapshot. This changes the source dependency version;
    it does not switch installation to PyPI. Includes a dependency release
    note in release_notes/fragments/20523.yaml.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Verified both branch tips using `git ls-remote` and GitHub's commit
    comparison API.
    - In a newly created openEuler/aarch64 container on the development
    host, verified that each of the four Dockerfiles differs from the
    release base only by the expected SHA substitution. All four affected
    `RUN` blocks pass `bash -n`; `git diff --check` and `bash
    tools/check_logger.sh` pass.
    - Ran `bash format.sh ci` locally: Ruff, codespell, typos, clang-format,
    markdownlint, actionlint, PNG, filename, Python package, forbidden
    import, boolean context manager, long function, and symbolic meta checks
    passed. The full command did not pass: native Windows hooks could not
    resolve `/bin/bash` for gitleaks/check-logger, and shellcheck is not
    installed. The logger check was subsequently run successfully in the
    Linux container.
    - No unit tests added for this dependency-pin-only change. Full Docker
    image builds and A2/A3 NPU runtime validation were not run; no further
    container/image validation was requested.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
    ---------
    
